WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.172
Welcome to Module 7.

00:00:02.172 --> 00:00:11.752
In this module, we are going to build one complete retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG, system from beginning to end.

00:00:11.752 --> 00:00:17.177
We will use one small student-support knowledge base throughout the module.

00:00:17.177 --> 00:00:22.207
That is important because I do not want the examples to feel disconnected.

00:00:22.207 --> 00:00:30.807
We will start with documents, clean them, split them into chunks, create embeddings, retrieve relevant evidence,

00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:35.451
build a grounded prompt, and finally generate an answer with sources.

00:00:36.055 --> 00:00:39.572
The first goal is not to use as many tools as possible.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.687
The first goal is to understand the architecture.

00:00:42.687 --> 00:00:50.737
Once the simple version works, we will move the same ideas into a vector database and then improve retrieval with

00:00:50.737 --> 00:00:53.352
filtering, keyword search, hybrid search, and reranking.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:59.867
By the end, you should be able to take a small document collection from your own work and build the same workflow

00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:02.027
yourself.
